From: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mt6789: q25: boot without the dev fastboot step

bootcmd printed "Marathon dev U-Boot: in fastboot" on the screen at every
boot and ran fastboot, whose gadget fails on this board, so the boot went
on to bootefi anyway. A release phone has no use for either.
---
diff --git a/board/mediatek/mtk-phone.env b/board/mediatek/mtk-phone.env
--- a/board/mediatek/mtk-phone.env
+++ b/board/mediatek/mtk-phone.env
@@ -19,13 +19,7 @@
 # Shortcut to enable USB serial gadget and disable bootretry
 serial_gadget=setenv stdin serial,button-kbd,usbacm; setenv stdout serial,vidconsole,usbacm; setenv stderr serial,vidconsole,usbacm; setenv bootretry -1; echo Enabled U-Boot console serial gadget
 
-# Marathon dev: this device has no usable input in U-Boot (volume keys are on
-# an MTK matrix keypad with no U-Boot driver, no serial cable), so the button
-# boot menu is unreachable. Enter fastboot on every boot instead — the host
-# runs `fastboot continue` to boot the OS, or `fastboot boot <img>` /
-# `fastboot flash <part> <img>`. This makes fastboot reliably reachable with
-# zero on-device input. (Revert to `bootefi bootmgr; ...` once bring-up settles.)
-bootcmd=echo '*** Marathon dev U-Boot: in fastboot. fastboot continue = boot OS ***'; run fastboot; run oneshot; run handoff; bootefi bootmgr; pause; run menucmd
+bootcmd=run oneshot; run handoff; bootefi bootmgr; pause; run menucmd
 
 # When entering the menu (either from button press or failed boot)
 # remap bootcmd so it will re-open the menu and we won't get stuck
